KZ3 patch 4022 (stage 3 fix, network pass 34): the pad layouts (4013 Modern / Custom) move gameplay actions in the
game's own action table instead of remapping the pad's buttons, so every menu keeps Cross = confirm, Circle = back.

Bug: under Modern, menus showed Square instead of Circle as back. 4013 remapped the buttons before the game
read them, so menus, legends and vehicles followed the gameplay layout. Now the remap of the host report is off,
the prompt atlas cells are no longer swapped (pad_remap_sig() = 0), and cellPadGetData (port 0, the game's thread)
writes the layout into the PlayerProfile's action table that ControlScheme::GetActionBinding (v1.00 0x4C79B4,
1.14 0x4D40B8) reads for every action and every action prompt. Modern is now per action (pad_actions.h): on-foot
actions move, vehicles / exo / turrets keep the scheme's own. KZ3_PAD_ACTIONS=0 turns the table writes off.
Host test: tools/net/test_pad_actions.c. Notes: the RE notes s.28.

